<apex:component ><h2 class="part">PART 4: CUSTOMER RESPONSIBILITY</h2>
<p><b>4.1 ROUTINE SERVICE &amp; MAINTENANCE</b> &#8211; To maintain coverage, the Customer must service the vehicle in accordance with the A-Protect Maintenance Schedule intervals:</p>
<table class="maint">
  <tr><td><b>CONVENTIONAL OIL</b></td><td><b>SYNTHETIC OIL</b></td></tr>
  <tr><td>4 Months / 8,000 km (whichever occurs first)</td><td>8 Months / 12,000 km (whichever occurs first)</td></tr>
</table>
<p>The Customer is solely responsible for retaining all maintenance documents to verify eligibility in the event of a claim. A-Protect allows a grace period of 30 days or 1,000 km for the completion of the required maintenance services. &#8220;Do-it-yourself&#8221; oil changes are not accepted. All services must be completed at a licensed repair facility. Submitted records must clearly indicate the service date, a detailed description of services performed, odometer reading, Vehicle Identification Number (VIN), and proof of payment. Failure to comply with the required maintenance schedule or documentation requirements may result in loss of eligibility for repair authorization under this Service Contract.</p>
<p><b>4.2 VEHICLE RECORDS &amp; DISCLOSURE</b> &#8211; During the active service period of this Service Contract, A-Protect may request supporting documentation from the Customer, including but not limited to: the original bill of sale or lease Service Contract; vehicle ownership or registration; and maintenance records with valid proof of payment.</p>
<p>If this Service Contract is purchased directly from A-Protect, the Customer must also submit a completed A-Protect Multi-Point Inspection Form within 30 days of purchase and before activation of the Service Contract. A-Protect reserves the right to defer or deny activation of this Service Contract if the required documentation is incomplete, inaccurate, or fails to meet the eligibility standards set forth herein. All requests and reviews performed under this section are administrative in nature and are intended solely to confirm vehicle eligibility and proper maintenance compliance.</p>
<p><b>4.3 CLAIMS PROCEDURE &amp; COMPLIANCE</b> &#8211; The Customer must comply with all Claim Procedures as outlined in this Service Contract. The Customer is responsible for all costs not covered by this Service Contract, including but not limited to fluid loss, shop supplies, inspections, diagnostic charges, machine shop charges, alignment, storage, and non-covered parts and labour.</p>


<h2 class="part">PART 5: CLAIMS PROCEDURE</h2>
<table class="contact"><tr>
  <td class="c1"><div class="clab">Contact A-Protect<br/>to report a claim</div>
      <div class="cval" style="margin-top:4px;">1(866) 660-6444</div>
      <div style="font-size:6.3pt; color:#3f4a5c;">or (416) 661-7444</div></td>
  <td class="c2"><div class="clab">Business hours</div>
      <div style="margin-top:5px; font-weight:bold;">Monday&#8211;Friday 9 AM &#8211; 5 PM EST</div></td>
  <td><div class="clab">Submit a claim online</div>
      <div style="margin-top:5px; font-weight:bold; color:#506590;">https://a-protectwarranty.com/report-a-claim/</div></td>
</tr></table>
<p><b>1&#160;&#160;Contact A-Protect to Report the Mechanical Breakdown.</b><span class="ind">In the event of a mechanical breakdown, the Customer must contact A-Protect during business hours to report the incident, submit a claim, and obtain instructions for vehicle delivery to an A-Protect Authorized Repair Facility. If the breakdown occurs within 200 km (one-way) of an Authorized Repair Facility, A-Protect reserves the right to require that the vehicle be transferred to that facility for repair. A-Protect will provide direction to the Customer regarding the assigned facility.</span></p>
<p><b>2&#160;&#160;Prior Authorization Required.</b><span class="ind">All diagnostics, repairs, or replacements to covered components must receive prior written or verbal approval from A-Protect. Any repair or replacement performed without such authorization&#8212;regardless of whether the affected component is otherwise listed as covered&#8212;will not be reimbursed or recognized under this Service Contract. The Customer must not authorize or complete repairs without A-Protect&#8217;s approval.</span></p>
<p><b>3&#160;&#160;Eligibility.</b><span class="ind">A-Protect will determine the status of coverage by assessing the approved Service Contract coverage amount minus any applicable diagnostic charges, consequential repairs, core charges, and miscellaneous fees. Labour time allowances for authorized repairs will be determined in accordance with Mitchell and ALLDATA industry-standard labour guides. A-Protect reserves the sole right and full discretion to decline any repair costs or estimates deemed unreasonable in comparison to available alternatives. A-Protect may also inspect the Covered Vehicle and select the parts or components to be used for any authorized repair.</span></p>
<p><b>4&#160;&#160;Roadside Coverage (Reimbursement).</b><span class="ind">The Customer must arrange roadside services through a third-party provider of their choice. To request reimbursement, a valid receipt (including proof of payment) must be submitted to A-Protect within fourteen (14) days of the occurrence. A-Protect is not responsible for coordinating or dispatching towing or roadside services, nor for arranging the vehicle&#8217;s transport to an Authorized Repair Facility or any other destination.</span></p>

<h2 class="part">PART 6: MAXIMUM AUTHORIZED REPAIR LIMIT</h2>
<p class="num">6.1 MAXIMUM AUTHORIZED REPAIR LIMIT – The liabilities of A-Protect under this service contract are determined solely by the coverage selected on the front page of the Application and the premium paid at the time of purchase. The maximum liability per claim shall not exceed half of the purchase price of the Covered Vehicle, and the total aggregate liability under this Contract shall not exceed the purchase price of the covered vehicle (excluding taxes, fees, and any aftermarket product). When multiple covered component failures are diagnosed at the same time, all related repairs will be considered a single authorized service event and applied toward the same claim limit. All amounts authorized and paid by A-Protect to the repair facility are inclusive of applicable taxes.</p>
<p class="num">6.2 DEDUCTIBLE – For each authorized repair event, the Customer shall be responsible for payment of the deductible amount indicated on the Registration Page of this Service Contract. The deductible must be paid directly to the A-Protect Authorized Repair Facility at the time of repair. If multiple covered components are repaired or replaced during the same authorized service visit, only one deductible shall apply. The deductible does not apply to any portion of costs that A-Protect determines to be outside the scope of this Service Contract, nor to non-covered parts, fluids, or incidental expenses. All authorized payments are administrative in nature and do not constitute the settlement of an insurance claim or indemnification for loss.</p>

<h2 class="part">PART 7: GENERAL PROVISIONS</h2>
<p class="num"><b>7.1 COVERAGE TERM</b> &#8211; The covered period will start on the purchase/lease date and/or on the delivery date of the vehicle. The commencement of coverage may be deferred if the vehicle is subject to an active manufacturer&#8217;s Service Contract, and such deferral is expressly stated on the application. The contract automatically terminates on the earlier of: a) the expiration date stated on the front page, or b) the date the vehicle reaches the stated mileage limit.</p>
<p class="num"><b>7.2 RENEWALS</b></p>
<p class="num ind"><b>Renewals</b> &#8211; The Service Contract may be renewed for an additional term if the Customer initiates and completes the renewal process at least thirty (30) days before the current Service Contract expires and meets all of the following conditions:</p>
<p class="num ind2">&#8226;&#160; Maintenance records are complete, current, and available for review.</p>
<p class="num ind2">&#8226;&#160; An A-Protect Multi-Point Inspection has been performed, and the inspection report has been submitted before the expiration of the existing Service Contract.</p>
<p class="num ind2">&#8226;&#160; All requested documents have been provided in full and verified by A-Protect.</p>
<p class="num ind2">&#8226;&#160; The Terms and Conditions in effect at the time of renewal will apply to the renewed Service Contract. A-Protect reserves the sole discretion to approve or deny any renewal application.</p>
<p class="num ind"><b>No Claims Double Your Term Renewal Offer</b> is available exclusively to Customers who purchased an eligible A-Protect 2-year, 3-year, or 4-year Service Contract package and meet all qualifying conditions. This renewal option allows the Customer to extend their Service Contract for an additional term&#8212;up to the length of the original term and up to a maximum value of CAD $5,000 on selected plans&#8212;for a processing fee of $149.00 CAD plus applicable taxes. To qualify, the Customer must contact A-Protect within 30 days before the expiry of the original Service Contract, have no claims of any kind (paid, denied, or pending), remain in full compliance with all Customer Responsibilities outlined in Part 4, and provide complete and verifiable service and maintenance records. All approved renewals under this program are final and are not eligible for refunds, transfers, or cancellations. A-Protect reserves the exclusive right to accept or decline any application and may offer a substitute Service Contract package of equal or lesser value if the vehicle no longer meets the eligibility criteria of the original Service Contract.</p>
<p class="num"><b>7.3 TRANSFERS</b> &#8211; This Service Contract may be transferred to a subsequent private purchaser of the Covered Vehicle, subject to prior written approval by A-Protect and compliance with all Terms and Conditions. A transfer request must be submitted within twenty (20) days of the vehicle ownership transfer and must include: a completed transfer application, a copy of the bill of sale, complete and verifiable maintenance records, transfer fee of $150.00 CAD plus applicable taxes. A-Protect may require, at the Customer&#8217;s expense, an oil change and/or vehicle inspection before approving the transfer. Approval of any transfer is subject to A-Protect&#8217;s administrative review of vehicle eligibility and maintenance compliance. Failure to provide required documentation or fees within the prescribed timeframe will result in a denial of the transfer request. If a transfer request is denied before approval, the transfer fee will be refunded.</p>
<p class="num"><b>7.4 CANCELLATIONS</b> &#8211; The Customer may request cancellation of this Service Contract through the original Selling Dealer within ten (10) days of the purchase date, provided no claims have been submitted, paid, or are pending. A-Protect reserves the right to cancel this Service Contract in the event of fraud, material misrepresentation, falsified documentation, improper vehicle use, non-payment by the Customer or Selling Dealer, or failure to meet eligibility requirements.</p>

<h2 class="part">PART 8: WARRANTY COVERAGE EXCLUSIONS</h2>
<p class="num">1. Any representations made other than what is expressly stated in this Contract are not covered.</p>
<p class="num">2. Non-compliance with the Terms and Conditions of this Service Contract, including but not limited to Customer Obligations and Claims Procedures, shall render coverage void.</p>
<p class="num">3. Parts that are not listed in this Contract, or that are expressly stated as exclusions, are not covered.</p>
<p class="num">4. Pre-existing problems or conditions, at A-Protect’s sole discretion, are excluded from coverage. Mechanical defects existing before the commencement of the Service Contract, or any problems or conditions diagnosed by A-Protect as pre-existing, are not covered.</p>
<p class="num">5. Parts or repairs that are covered in whole or in part by a Manufacturer’s Service Contract, or by any other Service Contract or insurance company, are excluded. This includes, but is not limited to, duplication of coverage, factory defects, recalls, and manufacturer campaigns or service bulletins.</p>
<p class="num">6. Vehicles used for hire or for the purpose of generating income are not covered. This includes, but is not limited to, ridesharing or food delivery services such as Uber, Lyft, or SkipTheDishes, courier or taxi services, limousine or driving school vehicles, emergency vehicles, competitive or race driving, and vehicles equipped with a snowplow.</p>
<p class="num">7. Vehicles with odometers that have been altered, tampered with, or not promptly repaired by the Customer are excluded from coverage.</p>
<p class="num">8. Vehicles pulling or carrying a payload exceeding one ton capacity are excluded unless prior approval has been obtained at the time of sale.</p>
<p class="num">9. Loss or damage resulting from after-factory modifications is not covered. Such modifications include, but are not limited to, installation of incorrect tires or rims, emission or exhaust alterations, fuel or ignition modifications, add-ons, high-performance parts or accessories, and snowplow additions.</p>
<p class="num">10. Repairs or replacements performed on covered parts without prior authorization from A-Protect are not eligible for coverage or reimbursement.</p>
<p class="num">11. Any repair or replacement of a part that has not exceeded the manufacturer’s field tolerances, or where a repair facility merely recommends, requires, or suggests replacement despite no actual failure, is not covered.</p>
<p class="num">12. Damage or loss caused by the Customer’s failure to take reasonable steps to protect the vehicle from further damage after a mechanical breakdown, including continuing to drive the vehicle or delaying repairs, is not covered.</p>
<p class="num">13. Miscellaneous or incidental costs necessary for a covered repair but not expressly listed in this Contract are excluded. This includes, but is not limited to, diagnostic charges, shop supplies, alignments, storage fees, computer or module programming, machine shop charges, fluid loss, adjustments, tune-ups, and regular servicing or maintenance.</p>
<p class="num">14. Failures or damage to covered parts caused by non-covered parts are not covered.</p>
<p class="num">15. Risks, losses, or damages resulting from unauthorized repairs, teardowns, or replacements are excluded, regardless of whether the affected component is a covered part.</p>
<p class="num">16. A-Protect is not responsible for delays in completing repairs or for losses resulting from such delays. This includes, but is not limited to, loss of vehicle use, time, profit, inconvenience, unavailability of parts, claim processing delays, or any other incidental or consequential losses resulting from a covered mechanical breakdown or failure.</p>
<p class="num">17. Clutch failure in manual or sequential transmissions is not classified as a transmission failure under this Service Contract.</p>
<p class="num">18. The timing belt is not covered as a standalone repair.</p>
<p class="num">19. The arrangement of third-party towing or roadside services for delivery of the vehicle to an A-Protect Authorized Repair Facility, or otherwise, is not covered.</p>
<p class="num">20. Damage or loss resulting from the Customer’s failure to perform maintenance in accordance with the A-Protect Maintenance Schedule is excluded.</p>
<p class="num">21. Any loss or damage caused by the lack of proper lubricants or coolants, including failure of water hoses, radiators, their connections, or transmission oil cooler lines, is not covered.</p>
<p class="num">22. Normal wear and tear is excluded. This includes, but is not limited to, repair or replacement of valves, valve seals, or piston rings causing high oil consumption or low compression, stretched timing chains, noisy lifters, and worn bearings.</p>
<p class="num">23. Repairs to carbonized or burned valves or seized piston rings are excluded.</p>
<p class="num">24. Risks, losses, or damage resulting from rust, corrosion, contamination, loss of fluids, lubricants, antifreeze, or refrigerants, improper type of engine oil or fuel, or any failure caused by burning oil or overheating, regardless of cause, are not covered.</p>
<p class="num">25. Gasoline exhaust systems and diesel exhaust components or fluids, including BlueTEC and AdBlue, are excluded from coverage.</p>
<p class="num">26. Emission system components, including but not limited to the evaporative emission system, exhaust gas recirculation system, positive crankcase ventilation system, and catalytic converters, are excluded.</p>
<p class="num">27. A-Protect shall not be liable for any damage, injury, or death, including any costs, expenses, or legal claims, suffered by any person, firm, or corporation, whether directly or indirectly caused by the vehicle or its components.</p>
<p class="num">28. Risks, losses, or damages resulting from misdiagnosis, improper repair, abuse, negligence, acts of God, repossession, collision, fire, theft, water damage, or freezing are not covered.</p>

